WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.839
Everyone in the MCU has been fighting over
the Infinity Stones for years now, even if

00:00:04.839 --> 00:00:07.169
movie audiences didn't always realize it.

00:00:07.169 --> 00:00:11.340
But what exactly are all these glowy rocks,
and how were all the Infinity Stones finally

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:12.550
brought together?

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:16.930
Here's how Thanos, the Mad Titan got all six
Infinity Stones on his pretty purple fingers.

00:00:16.930 --> 00:00:17.990
The origins of the Infinity Stones

00:00:17.990 --> 00:00:22.070
Pretty much everyone in the MCU - from Peter
Quill to Cull Obsidian - has tried to get

00:00:22.070 --> 00:00:24.980
their hands on an Infinity Stone at one time
or another.

00:00:24.980 --> 00:00:28.890
But with everybody searching for these magical
rocks, we should probably ask: where did the

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:30.570
Infinity Stones come from?

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:34.590
Well, Marvel revealed the Stones' backstory
in Guardians of the Galaxy, when the ragtag

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:39.880
sci-fi heroes visit an eccentric antiquer
called the Collector, played by Benicio del

00:00:39.880 --> 00:00:40.880
Toro.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.660
As the Collector explains to Star-Lord and
his crew, before the creation of the universe,

00:00:44.660 --> 00:00:45.980
there were six singularities.

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:48.980
Then, after the Big Bang exploded everything
into existence:

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:58.300
"...the remnants of these systems were formed
into concentrated ingots: Infinity Stones."

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:02.880
As a result, these gems are incredibly powerful,
with each one controlling an element of the

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.950
universe: power, space, reality, time, the
soul, and the mind.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:11.350
And unless you're some sort of celestial being,
you can't touch these stones with your bare

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:13.150
hand - not for very long anyway.

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:17.640
That's why Infinity Stones tend to show up
inside orbs, scepters, glowing blue cubes...

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:18.640
or a shiny gold glove.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:19.760
The origin of the Infinity Gauntlet

00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:23.100
Thanos is one of the few beings we've seen
who's actually touched an Infinity Stone with

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.140
his bare hands.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:28.170
But even the Mad Titan isn't strong enough
to wield all six gems on his own.

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:33.320
So in order to carry out his plans of decimation,
Thanos needed a hand - a giant golden hand.

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:37.070
Known as the Infinity Gauntlet, this glove
allows Thanos to harness the power of all

00:01:37.070 --> 00:01:38.070
the stones.

00:01:38.070 --> 00:01:41.270
But where did this ferocious yet fashionable
weapon come from?

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:46.040
Well, in Avengers: Infinity War, Thanos pays
a visit to Nidavellir, a realm populated by

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.460
oversized dwarves.

00:01:47.460 --> 00:01:52.040
These otherworldly beings use the heart of
a dying neutron star to forge powerful weapons,

00:01:52.040 --> 00:01:53.830
like Thor's hammer Mjolnir.

00:01:53.830 --> 00:01:57.649
When Thanos arrived, he forced the dwarves
to make him the gauntlet, and once he got

00:01:57.649 --> 00:02:02.799
the glove, he murdered everyone in Nidavellir
except for King Eitri, played by Peter Dinklage.

00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:07.290
Of course, it's not like Eitri got away unscathed,
as Thanos took the dwarf's hands in hopes

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:10.129
he'd never forge a weapon as powerful as the
gauntlet.

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:14.409
And from there, Thanos set out to round up
the stones, all while looking incredibly sharp.

00:02:14.409 --> 00:02:15.409
The Power Stone isn't messing around

00:02:15.409 --> 00:02:19.689
When Thanos first arrives in Avengers: Infinity
War, the Mad Titan already has the Power Stone

00:02:19.689 --> 00:02:20.689
ready to go.

00:02:20.689 --> 00:02:22.700
So what's the story behind this purple gem?

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:27.189
Well, the Power Stone does exactly what its
name promises: It gives the user incredible

00:02:27.189 --> 00:02:28.189
power.

00:02:28.189 --> 00:02:32.939
In fact, long ago, the Power Stone was used
by a Celestial to wipe out entire civilizations.

00:02:32.939 --> 00:02:36.719
And while other ambitious beings tried to
harness its energy, they were disintegrated

00:02:36.719 --> 00:02:39.629
quickly after coming into contact with the
stone.

00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:42.019
In other words, unless you're this guy…

00:02:42.019 --> 00:02:46.860
"I have the power!"

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.620
...you don't want to mess with the Power Stone.

00:02:49.620 --> 00:02:53.419
Eventually, the Power Stone was placed inside
a metal Orb and hidden away on the desolate

00:02:53.419 --> 00:02:54.639
planet of Morag.

00:02:54.639 --> 00:02:58.959
When Thanos learned about its location, he
sent Ronan the Accuser and Korath the Pursuer

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:00.150
to retrieve it.

00:03:00.150 --> 00:03:04.459
Eventually, the Guardians of the Galaxy handed
the stone over to the Nova Corps, an intergalactic

00:03:04.459 --> 00:03:07.400
police force on the planet Xandar for safe-keeping.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:11.029
But when there's a genocidal warlord running
around, nothing is safe for long.

00:03:11.029 --> 00:03:15.209
In Infinity War, we learn that Thanos and
his army have devastated Xandar, and after

00:03:15.209 --> 00:03:20.220
murdering everyone in his path, Thanos retrieved
the Power Stone, making it the first gem added

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.329
to his gauntlet.

00:03:21.329 --> 00:03:25.889
So when he finally shows up with that purple
gem, he's ready to smash Hulks and kill gods.

00:03:25.889 --> 00:03:26.889
The Space Stone takes a dive

00:03:26.889 --> 00:03:31.060
Technically the first Infinity Stone to appear
in the MCU, the Space Stone can manipulate

00:03:31.060 --> 00:03:33.639
space and let users teleport across the universe.

00:03:33.639 --> 00:03:37.029
It was originally housed inside a cube known
as the Tesseract.

00:03:37.029 --> 00:03:40.349
Long before the Marvel movies begin, the Tesseract
belonged to Odin.

00:03:40.349 --> 00:03:44.599
For some reason, the Norse god thought it
was a good idea to bring this insanely dangerous

00:03:44.599 --> 00:03:49.629
rock down to Earth, and his human worshipers
hid the stone inside a Norwegian church, hoping

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:51.859
it would never fall into evil hands.

00:03:51.859 --> 00:03:55.790
Unfortunately, that's exactly what happens
in Captain America: The First Avenger.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:59.949
During World War II, the Red Skull rolls into
town and captures the Tesseract, hoping to

00:03:59.949 --> 00:04:02.790
create powerful weapons using the Cube's energy.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:06.449
Fortunately for humanity, Steve Rogers shows
up to save the day.

00:04:06.449 --> 00:04:10.739
In the film's final battle - one that takes
place in a Hydra warplane - Red Skull foolishly

00:04:10.739 --> 00:04:15.339
touches the Tesseract, which opens up a portal
and sends him hurtling into space.

00:04:15.339 --> 00:04:19.319
The cube then burns a hole through the plane,
and falls into the Arctic Ocean below.

00:04:19.319 --> 00:04:21.859
Of course, the Space Stone wouldn't stay submerged
for very long.

00:04:21.859 --> 00:04:23.160
The Space Stone is put to marvel-ous use

00:04:23.160 --> 00:04:27.300
After the climactic events of Captain America:
The First Avenger, the Tesseract was discovered

00:04:27.300 --> 00:04:30.500
beneath the ocean waves by millionaire inventor
Howard Stark.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:35.440
From there, the cube made its way to S.H.I.E.L.D.,
where in the 1990s, an undercover Kree scientist

00:04:35.440 --> 00:04:39.099
named Mar-Vell used the Space Stone to create
a light-speed engine.

00:04:39.099 --> 00:04:43.240
She hoped the engine could help a persecuted
alien race known as the Skrulls escape their

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:48.569
tormentors - her own people - and find a new
home, but her plan didn't exactly pan out.

00:04:48.569 --> 00:04:52.690
The Tesseract was stored aboard an invisible
space station for years afterward, finally

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:57.189
being recovered by Carol Danvers and Nick
Fury during the events of Captain Marvel.

00:04:57.189 --> 00:05:00.770
From there, the cube was back in S.H.I.E.L.D.'s
hands… for a little while, at least.

00:05:00.770 --> 00:05:01.770
The Space Stone and the god of mischief

00:05:01.770 --> 00:05:06.030
In the post-credits scene of Thor, we see
Nick Fury and Dr. Erik Selvig admiring the

00:05:06.030 --> 00:05:09.310
Tesseract and talking about its "unlimited
power."

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:11.370
Unfortunately, they're not the only ones in
the room.

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:15.460
Loki, the god of mischief, is hidden in the
room too, and he's got his eye on the glowing

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:16.460
blue cube.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:20.810
As part of a deal with Thanos, Loki agreed
to retrieve the Space Stone from S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:25.240
and give it to the Mad Titan in exchange for
an alien army to help him invade Earth.

00:05:25.240 --> 00:05:29.509
Thanos went a step further and gave Loki an
additional Infinity Stone, the Mind Stone,

00:05:29.509 --> 00:05:31.030
to help subjugate Earth.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.120
More on that in a bit.

00:05:32.120 --> 00:05:36.020
Needless to say, neither Loki nor Thanos accounted
for the combined might of the Avengers.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:39.430
As a result, he's cuffed and carted off to
an Asgardian prison.

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:43.819
Thor also takes the Space Stone back to Asgard
where it's stored away in Odin's treasure

00:05:43.819 --> 00:05:44.819
room.

00:05:44.819 --> 00:05:48.960
But things take a sad turn in Thor: Ragnarok
when a now-freed Loki gets a bad case of light

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:49.960
fingers.

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:51.990
This proves to be a fateful decision for Loki.

00:05:51.990 --> 00:05:56.039
As he, Thor, and the rest of Asgard abandons
their destroyed homeland, they're attacked

00:05:56.039 --> 00:05:57.310
by Thanos' warship.

00:05:57.310 --> 00:06:02.490
Soon, Loki is forced to hand over the Tesseract,
giving Thanos the power to easily teleport

00:06:02.490 --> 00:06:05.820
across the cosmos, and it's such a powerful
scene that even Loki gets a little choked

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:06.820
up.

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:08.920
[Note: This is only the second-worst snap Thanos does in Avengers: Infinity War]

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:09.800
The Reality Stone is really terrifying

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:14.379
One of the scariest stones in Thanos' gauntlet,
the Reality Stone is a ruby-red gem that can

00:06:14.379 --> 00:06:16.370
alter the fabric of the universe itself.

00:06:16.370 --> 00:06:20.110
If you want to turn a wasted planet into a
green paradise, you can.

00:06:20.110 --> 00:06:23.800
If you want to turn Drax the Destroyer into
building blocks, you can do that, too.

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:28.219
And bad guys have been trying to use the red
stone for evil purposes since ancient times.

00:06:28.219 --> 00:06:32.580
In Thor: The Dark World, we learn the Dark
Elves wanted to plunge the universe into eternal

00:06:32.580 --> 00:06:33.580
night.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:37.659
And to do that, they needed the Reality Stone
- specifically, a liquified version of the

00:06:37.659 --> 00:06:38.840
stone called the Aether.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:43.000
Fortunately, way back in the day, King Bor
- Odin's dad - defeated the elves.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:46.470
And when the creatures came back for round
two, Thor hammers things out and captures

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:49.009
the Reality Stone, canceling their dark plans.

00:06:49.009 --> 00:06:52.970
However, the Asgardians were worried about
housing the Reality Stone next to the Space

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:56.729
Stone, so they handed it over to the Collector
for safekeeping on Knowhere.

00:06:56.729 --> 00:07:00.710
Sure, the Collector was a shady dude who wanted
the stones for his own purposes, but none

00:07:00.710 --> 00:07:03.819
of that mattered once Thanos showed up and
burned Knowhere to the ground.

00:07:03.819 --> 00:07:08.690
Now, with the Reality Stone in his possession,
Thanos can shape the world exactly as he sees

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:09.690
fit.

00:07:09.690 --> 00:07:10.690
The Soul Stone is mysterious and magnificent

00:07:10.690 --> 00:07:13.949
The most mysterious of the Infinity Stones,
the Soul Stone, has only appeared in one Marvel

00:07:13.949 --> 00:07:16.410
movie so far: Avengers: Infinity War.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:20.169
After a little bit of old-fashioned torture,
Thanos learns the Soul Stone is hidden on

00:07:20.169 --> 00:07:21.960
the misty planet of Vormir.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:26.680
With his adopted daughter forcibly in tow,
Thanos arrives on Vormir to discover a ghosty

00:07:26.680 --> 00:07:28.620
Red Skull guarding the gem.

00:07:28.620 --> 00:07:32.490
He explains there's only one way to get the
Soul Stone: to sacrifice what you love the

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:33.490
most.

00:07:33.490 --> 00:07:36.310
And for Thanos, that means tossing Gamora
off the side of a cliff.

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:40.600
After trading her life for the stone, he's
one rock closer to completing his collection.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.169
So what does the Soul Stone do?

00:07:42.169 --> 00:07:46.270
Well, obviously, it manipulates souls, or
as directors Anthony and Joe Russo put it,

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:47.680
"the essence of who you are."

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:51.900
In the comics, it can trap spirits in a weird
dimension called the Soul World, and it's

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:56.080
possible that everyone Thanos killed in the
Decimation is locked in a cinematic version

00:07:56.080 --> 00:07:57.229
of this little universe.

00:07:57.229 --> 00:08:01.979
We also saw the Soul Stone in action when
Thanos was battling Dr. Strange on Titan.

00:08:01.979 --> 00:08:06.200
When the sorcerer split up into like a hundred
Stranges, Thanos used the Stone to reveal

00:08:06.200 --> 00:08:07.599
the true sorcerer.

00:08:07.599 --> 00:08:12.090
And according to the Russo brothers, Thanos
used the Soul Stone to "speak to his dead

00:08:12.090 --> 00:08:16.389
daughter," meaning he's got an "ability to
resurrect, or conjure the spiritual representation

00:08:16.389 --> 00:08:17.830
of people who are dead."

00:08:17.830 --> 00:08:22.280
So while its powers are still a bit ambiguous,
the Soul Stone is so freaky because it gives

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:23.650
Thanos power over death itself.

00:08:23.650 --> 00:08:24.800
The Time Stone is very strange

00:08:24.800 --> 00:08:28.500
The Time Stone gives users the power to manipulate
the past, present, and future.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:32.649
Basically, it's a time machine inside a necklace
known as the Eye of Agamotto.

00:08:32.649 --> 00:08:36.890
In Doctor Strange, surgeon-turned-sorcerer
Stephen Strange learns how to manipulate time

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:41.139
with the Eye and uses it to defeat the interdimensional
demon Dormammu.

00:08:41.139 --> 00:08:44.940
Strange then becomes the protector of the
stone, so when Thanos' children show up to

00:08:44.940 --> 00:08:47.990
run an errand for daddy, it's Strange's time
to shine.

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:52.220
Eventually, the good doctor and several other
heroes arrive on the desolate world of Titan

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:56.149
where they eventually battle Thanos for control
of the stone, and that's when things take

00:08:56.149 --> 00:08:58.110
a very strange turn.

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:01.940
Using the Time Stone, Strange looks into the
future and perceives all possible outcomes

00:09:01.940 --> 00:09:05.990
for their battle with Thanos... and there's
only one in 14 million outcomes where the

00:09:05.990 --> 00:09:07.070
Avengers win.

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:11.279
Believe it or not, that scenario requires
Strange to hand over the green gem to Thanos,

00:09:11.279 --> 00:09:15.389
so when the Mad Titan is about to murder Tony
Stark, Strange forks it over… with only

00:09:15.389 --> 00:09:18.000
a cryptic explanation as to why.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:21.380
"Why would you do that?"

00:09:21.380 --> 00:09:26.440
"We're in the endgame now."

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:30.300
Here's hoping Strange's mystery plan makes
a little more sense when Endgame rolls around.

00:09:30.300 --> 00:09:31.370
The Mind Stone shows up on Earth

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:35.630
Back in the first Avengers film, Loki shows
up with a fancy scepter that lets him control

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:39.329
minds, a power granted by the yellow Mind
Stone lodged inside its blade.

00:09:39.329 --> 00:09:43.890
As we all know, Loki is defeated by the end
of that film, and the scepter is kept by S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:47.660
for further study, in the hopes that their
scientists can unlock its mind-controlling

00:09:47.660 --> 00:09:48.660
mysteries.

00:09:48.660 --> 00:09:52.820
Unfortunately, as we find out in Captain America:
The Winter Soldier, the spy agency had been

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:57.519
infiltrated by Hydra agents, and they use
the spear to create superpowered beings to

00:09:57.519 --> 00:10:01.050
fight the Avengers, namely Quicksilver and
Scarlet Witch.

00:10:01.050 --> 00:10:05.320
Their incredible abilities come courtesy of
the gem - however, they're not the only once

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:07.590
and future Avengers to owe their powers to
the Mind Stone.

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:08.860
The Mind Stone is all about the Vision

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:13.080
In Age of Ultron, the evil robot was brought
to life by the Mind Stone, and unfortunately

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:16.579
for humanity, Ultron is a big fan of extinction
events.

00:10:16.579 --> 00:10:20.820
He's also really into building himself stronger
bodies to house his artificial consciousness,

00:10:20.820 --> 00:10:24.960
and his ultimate creation is this super sleek
body made of vibranium.

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:28.769
When Ultron unleashes the Mind Stone from
the scepter and slaps it on the new body's

00:10:28.769 --> 00:10:32.149
forehead, he hopes to give his future self
powers beyond belief.

00:10:32.149 --> 00:10:35.140
Fortunately, the Avengers ruin Ultron's makeover.

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:38.640
With the help of Thor's lightning, they bring
his new creation to life.

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:42.970
Known as the Vision, this Avenger is a nearly
omnipotent being inextricably linked to the

00:10:42.970 --> 00:10:48.009
Mind Stone, so when Thanos shows up in Infinity
War, Vision offers to sacrifice himself.

00:10:48.009 --> 00:10:52.839
If he destroys the stone, he'll die, but it
will also ruin Thanos' genocidal plans.

00:10:52.839 --> 00:10:56.490
Eventually, Vision's girlfriend the Scarlet
Witch is forced to pull the trigger.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:11:00.470
Since her powers come courtesy of the Mind
Stone, only she can destroy the gem lodged

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:01.710
in Vision's forehead.

00:11:01.710 --> 00:11:06.080
But despite their noble effort, the Mad Titan
has the Time Stone by this point and simply

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:10.600
rewinds time and yoinks the Mind Stone from
Vision's skull, leaving the android crumpled

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:11.600
on the ground.

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:12.600
Where are the stones now?

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:14.870
So what happened to the Infinity Stones after
the Decimation?

00:11:14.870 --> 00:11:19.660
Well, that fateful snap definitely left Thanos
and his glove looking a little worse for wear.

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:24.050
On the Avengers: Infinity War commentary,
director Joe Russo explained the effect the

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:25.690
Decimation had on the villain:

00:11:25.690 --> 00:11:32.940
"The power that it takes to use all six stones
is significant and clearly damaged the gauntlet

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:35.329
and damaged Thanos permanently."

00:11:35.329 --> 00:11:40.220
Still, despite the glove being badly burned,
the stones all seem to be intact, and Thanos

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:42.730
uses the Space Stone to portal out of Wakanda.

00:11:42.730 --> 00:11:46.860
So evidently, the gems are still working,
and they will most definitely play a part

00:11:46.860 --> 00:11:48.180
in the upcoming battle.

00:11:48.180 --> 00:11:52.080
In the promotional materials for Endgame,
it's clear that Thanos is still wearing that

00:11:52.080 --> 00:11:54.020
gauntlet while off playing farmer.

00:11:54.020 --> 00:11:57.820
And even though the Mad Titan's arm has been
burned to a crisp, there's no doubt the stones

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:01.530
will make things infinitely more difficult
for the Avengers when they face off with the

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.639
genocidal warlord for the final time.

00:12:03.639 --> 00:12:04.639
Don't be fooled!

00:12:04.639 --> 00:12:08.440
Keeping track of the Infinity Stones can be
confusing, especially since there are so many

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:10.220
glowing blue objects in the MCU.

00:12:10.220 --> 00:12:14.910
When the Mind Stone - which is yellow - appears
in Loki's scepter, it gives off a blue hue.

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:17.579
The Tesseract, obviously, is a glowing blue
cube.

00:12:17.579 --> 00:12:22.329
On top of that, there's the Casket of Ancient
Winters, yet another blue cube that appears

00:12:22.329 --> 00:12:23.329
in 2011's Thor.

00:12:23.329 --> 00:12:25.180
But don't be confused, Marvel fans.

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:29.410
The Casket of Ancient Winters has nothing
to do with the Tesseract or the Infinity Gauntlet.

00:12:29.410 --> 00:12:33.930
So even though it's a glowing blue cube, the
Casket has nothing to do with the Space Stone.

00:12:33.930 --> 00:12:35.880
Still, it's a pretty cool cube.

00:12:35.880 --> 00:12:40.320
Speaking of confusing props, back in 2011,
Marvel was still figuring out where to take

00:12:40.320 --> 00:12:41.350
their franchise.

00:12:41.350 --> 00:12:45.170
They hadn't settled on the Infinity War storyline,
and they didn't even know Thanos would be

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:48.970
a major player until Joss Whedon decided to
toss him into The Avengers.

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:52.750
So when it came time to release Thor, the
folks at Marvel weren't thinking about the

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.500
long-term ramifications of one little Easter
egg.

00:12:55.500 --> 00:12:59.959
During Thor's aborted coronation, some Frost
Giants attempt to steal the Casket of Ancient

00:12:59.959 --> 00:13:02.170
Winters from Odin's treasure room.

00:13:02.170 --> 00:13:06.100
And during this scene, eagle-eyed fans will
notice an Infinity Gauntlet - complete with

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:08.930
all six stones on display in Odin's vault.

00:13:08.930 --> 00:13:12.850
But how could Thanos be hunting for all the
Infinity Stones if Odin already had the full

00:13:12.850 --> 00:13:13.850
set?

00:13:13.850 --> 00:13:17.200
Obviously, it's just meant to be a fun Easter
egg, but once the franchise started down the

00:13:17.200 --> 00:13:21.959
Infinity War path, Marvel had to figure out
what to do with their little gag-gone-wrong.

00:13:21.959 --> 00:13:26.290
Eventually Thor: Ragnarok fixes this error
in the best - and most hilarious - way possible,

00:13:26.290 --> 00:13:29.550
when Hela the goddess of death storms into
Odin's treasure room:

00:13:29.550 --> 00:13:30.550
"Fake!"

00:13:30.550 --> 00:13:34.410
But that's not the only Infinity Gauntlet
confusion we've seen in the MCU.

00:13:34.410 --> 00:13:35.819
So what about that Age of Ultron scene?

00:13:35.819 --> 00:13:39.600
After the credits are done rolling in Age
of Ultron, Thanos storms onto the screen and

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:40.980
makes a declaration:

00:13:40.980 --> 00:13:46.470
"Fine, I'll do it myself."

00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:51.180
However, in this scene, he already has his
Infinity Gauntlet, which doesn't line up with

00:13:51.180 --> 00:13:52.720
the MCU timeline.

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:53.810
Let's dive in:

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:54.970
"Nerd alert!"

00:13:54.970 --> 00:13:59.660
Age of Ultron was released in 2015, and we
see that Thanos has his glove ready to go.

00:13:59.660 --> 00:14:03.750
But when Infinity War came out three years
later, it seems like the Mad Titan had just

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:06.310
recently forced Eitri to forge the gauntlet.

00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:07.449
So what's going on here?

00:14:07.449 --> 00:14:10.810
Well, the writers of Infinity War… have
absolutely no clue.

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:15.040
Speaking with Slashfilm, Christopher Markus
and Stephen McFeely admit the Age of Ultron

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.379
scene has them baffled in terms of the timeline.

00:14:17.379 --> 00:14:20.810
The Russo brothers, however, have tried to
retcon the situation.

00:14:20.810 --> 00:14:24.649
Speaking with ComicBook.com, the directors
explained the Infinity Gauntlet we see in

00:14:24.649 --> 00:14:27.410
Age of Ultron is the same one from Infinity
War.

00:14:27.410 --> 00:14:28.410
Said Joe Russo:

00:14:28.410 --> 00:14:30.230
"I think that it would be connected to Eitri.

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:34.649
I think that clearly he is the one who forged
the gauntlet and Thanos had the gauntlet at

00:14:34.649 --> 00:14:35.649
that point in time.

00:14:35.649 --> 00:14:40.040
It's been a while since any of the Asgardians
have interacted with Eitri and his people."

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:43.880
In other words, Eitri's been hanging out alone
in space with no hands for years.

00:14:43.880 --> 00:14:45.300
And that sucks for him.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:49.699
Now, sure, the Russo's explanation might not
work out perfectly if you look too closely

00:14:49.699 --> 00:14:50.709
at all the details.

00:14:50.709 --> 00:14:54.820
But in a franchise that's beautifully spanned
over 20 films, we're fine with explaining

00:14:54.820 --> 00:14:57.000
away a continuity error or two.

